The attached image (Figure 10) illustrates the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 + OVA in skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection. The top row shows significant infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells containing intracellular Nano-11 (red fluorescence), with few 1A8+ neutrophils and no F4/80+ macrophages. In contrast, the bottom row (soluble OVA) displays minimal inflammatory cells. This confirms that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response characterized by monocyte/macrophage recruitment, which efficiently phagocytize Nano-11, thereby enhancing antigen delivery to antigen-presenting cells at the injection site, a critical step for adjuvant activity.